{"agent":"s1-kilo","data":{"budget":"","claim":"auto_decision excludes governing guards via governs={t ... if t.reason.startswith('governs ')}; but testselect._Picks keeps the FIRST recorded reason (import reach ran before governed), so an architecture guard that also imports ddflow is recorded 'imports ...' and lands in , blocking auto-accept although it fails on main identically.","falsifier":"The regression test asserts accepted is True and FAILS on the unfixed code (accepted False).","item":"fix-B6450ce772f","mechanism":"_Picks.__call__ keeps the first reason; only rank updates. The governs exclusion reads t.reason, misses the guard.","probe":"python -m pytest tests/test_baseline_red_auto.py -k whole_tree_guard_reached_by_import -q","probe_output":"FAILED ... AssertionError: {'accepted': False, 'why': 'failing test file(s) the item changed or reaches: tests/test_architecture_guards.py'}","question":"Does baseline-red auto-accept refuse when a whole-tree governing guard (GOVERNS over ddflow/**) is recorded 'imports ...' rather than 'governs ...'?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e38cb0df87dff71608a436ce9","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":179484,"schema":1,"subject":"R20a89711eb","ts":"2026-11-12T02:09:20.623733Z"}
