{"agent":"s1-kilo","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new exclusion is keyed only on `TS.governed(tree, sorted(changed), files)`, so any failing test file whose declared `GOVERNS` globs match a changed path is added to `excluded`. This is broader than “whole-tree architecture guard” and, on the non-full path, it removes the reach guard that is the only protection against a new offender (the comment immediately below says the non-full path does not also consult `uncompared`). For example, with a red baseline, a changed file `ddflow/api/family_schema.py`, and a failing test `tests/test_family_schema.py` that declares `GOVERNS = (\"ddflow/api/family_schema.py\",)` but is selected by testselect with the import reason, the new line puts that test file into `excluded`. If the item introduces a new assertion failure in that test, the non-full path still sees `reached - excluded` as empty and returns `accepted=True`, auto-accepting a regression in the very test that governs the changed file. The second added test only proves that a non-matching `GOVERNS` glob still blocks; it does not constrain the overbroad matching case.","digest":"203158df700a394c","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/gates/baseline.py:275","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/gates/baseline.py:275"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":4030,"diff_sha":"5d715e3b173efb46b03f7c46507fd3f07df517739d1218a83c55a4c877ff7c47","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B6450ce772f","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":91.5,"family":"alibaba","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"8df4f13150981af7","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B6450ce772f.critic.grok-4.7.20261112T022323Z-a10bd427.jsonl","reason":"","r